<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Austro-Turkish War (1716–1718)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1716–1718</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Austro-Turkish War of 1716 to 1718 was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> monarchy and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> entered in support of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, then at war with the Ottomans. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-eugene-of-savoy">Prince Eugene of Savoy</a> won a decisive victory at Petrovaradin in 1716, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timisoara">Temeswar</a> the same year and captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a> in 1717. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-passarowitz">Treaty of Passarowitz</a> in 1718 gave Austria the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banat">Banat</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> with Belgrade, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oltenia">Oltenia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/austro-turkish-war-1716-1718.jpg" alt="Austro-Turkish War (1716–1718)" width="320" height="261" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georg Philipp Rugendas the Elder · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georg-philipp-rugendas-the-elder-1716-battle-of-petrovaradin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
